Attribution for the PKWARE DCL "implode" format facts
=====================================================

`src/explode.rs` implements the PKWARE Data Compression Library "implode"
format from public documentation. The implementation is project-authored and
is not a translation of any other decoder.

One artefact is derived from a licensed source and is recorded here for
transparency: the format's three fixed Huffman codebooks (the bit lengths of
the 256 literal codes, the 16 length codes and the 64 distance codes) together
with the length base and length extra-bit tables. Those are constants defined
by the format itself, not authored code, and were read from the format
description distributed with Mark Adler's `blast`:

  Upstream: https://github.com/madler/zlib/tree/master/contrib/blast
  File:     blast.c, version 1.3, 24 Aug 2013
  Author:   Mark Adler
  Licence:  zlib

`blast.c` in turn credits the reverse-engineered format description posted by
Ben Rudiak-Gould to comp.compression on 13 August 2001, which is the primary
public specification. The known-answer vector used by this crate's tests
(`00 04 82 24 25 8f 80 7f` decoding to "AIAIAIAIAIAIA") is published in the
same comment block.

The tables are restated here in a different form (explicit
`(bit length, run length)` pairs rather than the packed nibble encoding used
upstream) and their completeness is verified by a unit test.

